@*
    Unsubscribe.razor
    Purpose: Public landing page for the one-click unsubscribe link carried by every
    newsletter message. [REQ-FN-032 / BRD-59]

    Route: /unsubscribe/{Token}
    Layout: FullWidthLayout (public shell, no blog sidebar — matches /verify/{token})

    ANONYMOUS BY DESIGN — deliberately carries NO @attribute [Authorize]. The link is
    followed out of a mail client by someone who may have no account at all, and an
    unsubscribe that demands a sign-in is not an unsubscribe. The opaque per-subscriber
    token in the route IS the authorisation; nothing here reads the current identity.

    THE DEFECT THIS PAGE FIXES: NewsletterSvc has mailed {BaseUrl}/unsubscribe/{token}
    since the newsletter feature shipped, but no page was ever routed there, so every
    issue already delivered carried an unsubscribe link that answered HTTP 404 with a
    zero-byte body. That is a compliance failure, not a cosmetic one.

    States (exactly one card body renders):
      loading             — the token has not been applied yet
      unsubscribed        — the token resolved and the subscriber was opted out now
      alreadyUnsubscribed — the token resolved but the subscriber was already off the list
      invalid             — the token resolved to nobody, or the request could not be processed

    The invalid state never says whether the token existed, so the route cannot be used to
    test guessed tokens against the subscriber list.

    Colour comes from TrBlazeUI semantic tokens only (text-primary / text-destructive and
    the Alert variants) — no hardcoded hex values, so all site themes x light/dark work.

    The heading is a raw <h1> with utility classes rather than <TypographyH1>, for the same
    reason VerifyEmail.razor gives: TypographyH1 bakes in text-4xl and .text-4xl is emitted
    after .text-2xl in trblazeui.css, so a Class override loses on equal specificity.
*@
@page "/unsubscribe/{Token}"
@layout FullWidthLayout

<SiteBrandTitle Page="@PageHeading" Separator=" · " />

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg py-8" data-testid="unsubscribe-page">

    <Card data-testid="unsubscribe-card">
        <CardContent Class="p-8 text-center">

            @if (State == UnsubscribeState.Loading)
            {
                <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 py-12" data-testid="unsubscribe-loading">
                    <Spinner Size="SpinnerSize.Large" Class="text-primary" />
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Processing your unsubscribe request&hellip;</p>
                </div>
            }
            else if (State == UnsubscribeState.Unsubscribed)
            {
                <div data-testid="unsubscribe-done">
                    <div class="mb-6 flex justify-center">
                        <LucideIcon Name="circle-check" Size="72" Class="text-primary" />
                    </div>

                    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">You have been unsubscribed</h1>

                    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="unsubscribe-summary">
                        The address this link belongs to will no longer receive the TechieBlog newsletter.
                    </p>

                    <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Success" Class="mt-6 text-left" data-testid="unsubscribe-success-alert">
                        <LucideIcon Name="circle-check" Size="16" />
                        <AlertTitle>Removed from the mailing list</AlertTitle>
                        <AlertDescription>
                            It takes effect immediately &mdash; an issue already on its way may still arrive.
                            Nothing else about your account or comments has changed.
                        </AlertDescription>
                    </Alert>
                </div>
            }
            else if (State == UnsubscribeState.AlreadyUnsubscribed)
            {
                <div data-testid="unsubscribe-already">
                    <div class="mb-6 flex justify-center">
                        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="72" Class="text-primary" />
                    </div>

                    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Already unsubscribed</h1>

                    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="unsubscribe-summary">
                        This address is already off the newsletter list, so nothing was changed.
                    </p>

                    <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Info" Class="mt-6 text-left" data-testid="unsubscribe-already-alert">
                        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
                        <AlertTitle>Nothing left to do</AlertTitle>
                        <AlertDescription>
                            You will not receive further issues. The link stays valid, so you can open it
                            again at any time without any effect.
                        </AlertDescription>
                    </Alert>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div data-testid="unsubscribe-invalid">
                    <div class="mb-6 flex justify-center">
                        <LucideIcon Name="circle-alert" Size="72" Class="text-destructive" />
                    </div>

                    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">This link is not valid</h1>

                    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="unsubscribe-summary">
                        Nothing has been changed.
                    </p>

                    <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Danger" Class="mt-6 text-left" data-testid="unsubscribe-invalid-alert">
                        <LucideIcon Name="circle-alert" Size="16" />
                        <AlertTitle>Unsubscribe failed</AlertTitle>
                        <AlertDescription>@ErrorMessage</AlertDescription>
                    </Alert>

                    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="unsubscribe-invalid-help">
                        Open the link straight from a recent newsletter rather than retyping it &mdash; the
                        token is long and a truncated copy will not resolve. If it still fails, reach us
                        through the <a class="underline" href="/about">about page</a> and we will remove the
                        address by hand.
                    </p>
                </div>
            }

            @if (State != UnsubscribeState.Loading)
            {
                <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3" data-testid="unsubscribe-actions">
                    <Button Href="/newsletters" Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline" data-testid="unsubscribe-archive">
                        Read the archive
                    </Button>
                    <Button Href="/" data-testid="unsubscribe-home">
                        <LucideIcon Name="arrow-left" Size="16" />
                        <span class="ml-2">Back to TechieBlog</span>
                    </Button>
                </div>

                <Separator Class="my-6" />

                <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="unsubscribe-footnote">
                    Changed your mind? You can subscribe again from the newsletter box on any page.
                </p>
            }

        </CardContent>
    </Card>
</div>
